.TH XUZZEL 1 "September 2026" "xuzzel 1.15.0-x11.1"
.SH NAME
xuzzel \- X11 application launcher and dmenu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xuzzel
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xuzzel
is an X11 launcher and picker retaining dmenu's Xlib/Xft drawing and event-loop foundation. In launcher mode it discovers freedesktop desktop entries. With
.B --dmenu
it reads newline-delimited choices from standard input and writes the selected choice to standard output.
.PP
Command-line and configuration names track fuzzel 1.15.0 where an X11 equivalent exists. Command-line values override configuration. This is an independent X11 program and installs no fuzzel alias.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -d , " --dmenu"
Dmenu mode.
.TP
.B --dmenu0
Dmenu mode with NUL-separated input.
.TP
.BI --config= PATH
Use configuration file. /dev/null disables configuration.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate configuration and exit.
.TP
.BI --override= [SECTION.]KEY=VALUE
Override a configuration value. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR -f , " --font=" FONT
Fontconfig font description.
.TP
.BR -p , " --prompt=" TEXT
Prompt text.
.TP
.BI --placeholder= TEXT
Placeholder is available through the configuration file.
.TP
.BR -l , " --lines=" N
Maximum result rows.
.TP
.BR -w , " --width=" N
Width, measured approximately in line-height units.
.TP
.BR -a , " --anchor=" POSITION
One of center, top, bottom, left, right and combinations such as top-left.
.TP
.BR -o , " --output=" OUTPUT
X11 equivalent: numeric Xinerama monitor index. Named Wayland outputs are accepted but cannot be resolved.
.TP
.BI --match-mode= MODE
exact, fzf, or fuzzy. fuzzy currently uses the fzf subsequence scorer.
.TP
.BR -D , " --dpi-aware=" MODE
Accepted. Xft/fontconfig and X server DPI determine scaling.
.TP
.B --password[=CHAR]
Hide entered text using bullets, or an ASCII asterisk when a character is supplied.
.TP
.BI --select= TEXT
Initially select exact display text.
.TP
.BI --select-index= INDEX
Initially select zero-based index.
.TP
.B --minimal-lines
Shrink result area to result count.
.TP
.B --hide-prompt
Hide prompt.
.TP
.B --hide-before-typing
Hide result rows until input exists.
.TP
.B --counter
Show match/total counter.
.TP
.B --auto-select
Accept automatically when exactly one result exists.
.TP
.B --no-sort
Keep source order. Equivalent to sort-result=no in configuration.
.TP
.B --no-mouse
Disable pointer selection and ButtonPress event subscription. Equivalent to enable-mouse=no in configuration.
.TP
.BI --search= TEXT
Initial search text.
.TP
.BI --cache= PATH
History path. Dmenu mode only uses history when explicitly set.
.TP
.BI --launch-prefix= COMMAND
Prefix launcher commands.
.TP
.B --index
Print zero-based input index rather than selected text in dmenu mode.
.TP
.BR -b , " --background-color=" RRGGBB[AA]
Set background. Alpha is accepted but ignored by default X11 visual.
.TP
.BR -t , " --text-color=" RRGGBB[AA]
Set result text color. The prompt/input/match/selection/counter/border color options from fuzzel 1.15.0 are also accepted.
.TP
.BR -B , " --border-width=" N
Border width.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print help.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version"
Print version.
.SH INPUT
Enter accepts selection. Shift+Enter accepts typed text. Escape exits 1. Up/Down and PageUp/PageDown navigate. Tab inserts selection. Ctrl+A/E/B/F/P/N/H/D/U/K/W and Ctrl+V provide Emacs-style editing and clipboard paste.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Search order is $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fuzzel/fuzzel.ini, then $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xuzzel/xuzzel.ini, corresponding paths below each $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS entry, with ~/.config used when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset. See xuzzel.ini(5).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on selection or successful validation, 1 on cancellation, greater than zero on errors.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Wayland-only layer, namespace, output naming, focus-loss protocol behavior, fractional protocol scaling, IME protocol, transparency/blur, gamma-correct blending, rounded clipping, action submenus, and startup-notification semantics have no exact X11 equivalent. Launcher icons support PNG and SVG, freedesktop theme inheritance, hicolor, pixmaps, and absolute paths. The xuzzel extension --icon-size=PIXELS overrides row-based sizing; fuzzel 1.15 documents no icon-size CLI option. Messages occupy one clipped row; message-mode wrapping/expansion is not implemented or accepted.
.SH ATTRIBUTION
Drawing and event-loop structure derive from dmenu 5.4, Copyright 2006-2024 suckless.org, under the repository LICENSE. Fuzzel 1.15.0 manuals and behavior were used as compatibility references; no fuzzel source is incorporated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xuzzel.ini (5),
.BR dmenu (1)
